/-!
# Analytically unramified primes with discrete valuation localization

Stacks Tag 032Z (Lemma 10.162.11 of the Stacks Project).

Throughout, all rings are commutative with unit. Let `(R, m)` be a Noetherian
local ring.

Let `R` be a Noetherian local ring and let `p ⊂ R` be a prime ideal. Assume:

1. the localization `R_p` is a discrete valuation ring, and
2. the prime `p` is analytically unramified, i.e. `R^ / p R^` is reduced,
   where `R^ = lim_n R / m^n` is the `m`-adic completion of `R`.

Then for every associated prime `q` of the `R^`-module `R^ / p R^`, the local
ring `(R^)_q` is a discrete valuation ring.

## Definitions

- Completion: the `m`-adic completion `R^ = lim_n R / m^n`. In Mathlib this is
  `AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R`, which carries a `CommRing`
  structure and an `Algebra R` structure; the canonical (faithfully flat local)
  ring homomorphism `R → R^` is `algebraMap R (AdicCompletion m R)`.

- For an ideal `I ⊂ R`, the ideal `I R^` of `R^` generated by the image of `I`
  is `Ideal.map (algebraMap R R^) I`.

- Discrete valuation ring: `IsDiscreteValuationRing` (a local PID that is not a
  field; equivalently a one-dimensional regular local domain). Note it carries an
  `IsDomain` assumption, so to state that a localization is a DVR we also assert
  the relevant `IsDomain` instance.

- Analytically unramified prime: `p` is analytically unramified iff `R^ / p R^`
  is reduced (`IsReduced`). This is the form used in the statement; it is
  equivalent, via `(R/p)^ ≅ R^ / p R^`, to `(R/p)^` being reduced.

- Associated prime of a module: `IsAssociatedPrime q M` means `q` is a prime
  ideal which is the annihilator of some element `x : M`. Here `M = R^ / p R^`
  viewed as an `R^`-module, and `q : Ideal R^`.

- Localization at a prime: `Localization.AtPrime q` is `(R^)_q`.
-/

@[expose] public section

/-- The `m`-adic completion `R^` of a (Noetherian local) ring `R`, where
`m` is its maximal ideal. -/
@[ega "0 10.2.3" "special case",
  ega "0 17.3.8.1" "special case",
  ega "0 19.8.3",
  ega "0 7.3.1" "special case",
  ega "II 8.10.3",
  ega "III 7.5.1" "Â, special case",
  ega "IV 8.11.4",
  sga "1 II 4.14" "special case",
  sga "1 IV 3.1" "maximal-ideal completion",
  sga "3 VIIB 2.6" "partial",
  sga "3 VIIB 4.1.1" "partial",
  sga "3 X 4.0",
  sga "7 VI 4.1(d)"]
noncomputable abbrev mCompletion (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] : Type _ :=
  AdicCompletion (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R) R

/-- The ideal `p R^` of the completion generated by the image of `p ⊂ R`. -/
noncomputable abbrev pCompletion {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (p : Ideal R) :
    Ideal (mCompletion R) :=
  Ideal.map (algebraMap R (mCompletion R)) p

/-- `p` is analytically unramified: the completion of `R/p`, identified with
`R^ / p R^`, is reduced. -/
@[sga "1 I 9.4" "more general"]
def AnalyticallyUnramifiedPrime {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] (p : Ideal R) : Prop :=
  IsReduced (mCompletion R ⧸ pCompletion p)

/-!
## Proof sketch: decomposition into sub-lemmas

The informal proof runs:

1. **(`assoc = minimal`)** Since `R^/pR^` is reduced (`hunr`) and `R^` is
   Noetherian, the associated primes of `R^/pR^` are exactly its minimal primes,
   which are exactly the minimal primes over `pCompletion p`. Hence the
   associated prime `q` is minimal over `pCompletion p`; in particular
   `pCompletion p ≤ q`.

2. **(`max ideal = p (R^)_q`)** Because `q` is *minimal* over `pCompletion p`,
   in the localization `(R^)_q` the extension of `pCompletion p` is the (unique)
   maximal ideal `q (R^)_q` *up to radical*; reducedness then forces equality, so
   the maximal ideal of `(R^)_q` equals `pCompletion p · (R^)_q`.

3. **(`uniformizer`)** `R_p` is a DVR (`hdvr`), so `p R_p` is principal: there is
   `x ∈ R` whose image in `R_p` generates `p R_p`. The image of `x` in `(R^)_q`
   generates its maximal ideal (combine with step 2 and `p (R^)_q = (x) (R^)_q`).

4. **(`nonzerodivisor`)** `x` is a nonzerodivisor in `R` (its image in the domain
   `R_p` is nonzero), and `R → R^` is faithfully flat, so the image of `x` is a
   nonzerodivisor in `R^`, hence in `(R^)_q`.

5. **(`assemble`)** `(R^)_q` is a Noetherian local ring whose maximal ideal is
   nonzero and generated by a single nonzerodivisor; equivalently it is a
   one-dimensional regular local domain, i.e. a DVR. This yields both the
   `IsDomain` instance (goal A) and `IsDiscreteValuationRing` (goal B).

Below we record these as named lemmas (each unproved, with its argument), and
assemble them in `exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_atPrime_of_analyticallyUnramified`. The hard,
load-bearing Mathlib pieces are: faithful flatness of `AdicCompletion` (step 4) and the
"associated = minimal in a reduced Noetherian ring" fact (step 1).
-/

section Sketch

variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
variable (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime]

/- **L1 (associated ⇒ minimal).** In the reduced Noetherian ring `R^/pR^`, the
associated primes of the module `R^/pR^` are exactly the minimal primes, i.e. the
minimal primes over `pCompletion p`. Hence any associated prime `q` is minimal
over `pCompletion p`.

*Argument.* A reduced Noetherian ring has no embedded associated primes: its set
of associated primes equals its set of minimal primes (Mathlib:
`IsReduced` ⇒ the zero ideal is radical ⇒ `associatedPrimes` of the ring coincide
with `minimalPrimes`). Pulling back along the quotient map `R^ → R^/pR^`, the
associated primes of `R^/pR^` (as an `R^`-module) correspond to primes of `R^`
containing `pCompletion p`, and the minimal ones among these are the minimal
primes over `pCompletion p`. -/
/-- Helper: in a reduced commutative ring, an associated prime of the ring
(viewed as a module over itself) is a minimal prime.

*Argument.* Write `q' = √(ann a)` with `a ≠ 0` (else `q' = ⊤`). Take any prime
`J ≤ q'`. First `a ∉ J`: otherwise `a ∈ J ≤ q' = √(ann a)` gives `a^{n+1} = 0`,
so `a = 0` by reducedness. Then for `t ∈ q'` we have `t^n a = 0 ∈ J`, and `J`
prime with `a ∉ J` forces `t^n ∈ J`, hence `t ∈ J`. So `q' ≤ J` and `q'` is
minimal. -/
@[ega "IV 3.2.1" "partial"]
lemma assoc_prime_mem_minimalPrimes_of_isReduced {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsReduced A]
    {q' : Ideal A} (h : IsAssociatedPrime q' A) : q' ∈ minimalPrimes A := by
  obtain ⟨hp, a, ha⟩ := h
  have hmem : ∀ s : A, s ∈ (⊥ : Ideal A).colon {a} ↔ s * a = 0 := by
    intro s; rw [Submodule.mem_colon_singleton]; simp [Submodule.mem_bot, smul_eq_mul]
  rw [show minimalPrimes A = (⊥ : Ideal A).minimalPrimes from rfl]
  refine ⟨⟨hp, bot_le⟩, ?_⟩
  intro J hJ hJq
  obtain ⟨hJp, -⟩ := hJ
  have ha0 : a ≠ 0 := by
    rintro rfl
    apply hp.ne_top
    rw [ha, Ideal.radical_eq_top, Ideal.eq_top_iff_one, hmem]; ring
  have haJ : a ∉ J := by
    intro haJ
    have hmemq : a ∈ q' := hJq haJ
    rw [ha] at hmemq
    obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := hmemq
    rw [hmem] at hn
    have hpow : a ^ (n + 1) = 0 := by
      rw [pow_succ]; exact hn
    exact ha0 (IsReduced.eq_zero a ⟨n + 1, hpow⟩)
  rw [ha]
  intro t ht
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := ht
  rw [hmem] at hn
  have htn : t ^ n ∈ J := by
    have hmm : t ^ n * a ∈ J := hn ▸ J.zero_mem
    rcases hJp.mem_or_mem hmm with h1 | h2
    · exact h1
    · exact absurd h2 haJ
  exact hJp.mem_of_pow_mem n htn

/-- Helper: an associated prime `q` of `S ⧸ I` (as an `S`-module) is the comap
along `S → S ⧸ I` of an associated prime `q'` of the ring `S ⧸ I` over itself.

*Argument.* The `S`-annihilator of `x : S ⧸ I` equals the comap of the
`(S ⧸ I)`-annihilator of `x` (since `s • x = (mk s) * x`); taking radicals gives
`q = comap (mk I) q'` with `q' = √(ann x)`. As `mk I` is surjective and
`ker (mk I) = I ≤ q`, primality of `q` transfers to `q'`. -/
lemma exists_assoc_prime_quotient_comap {S : Type*} [CommRing S] {I : Ideal S} {q : Ideal S}
    (hq : IsAssociatedPrime q (S ⧸ I)) :
    ∃ q' : Ideal (S ⧸ I),
      IsAssociatedPrime q' (S ⧸ I) ∧ q = Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) q' := by
  obtain ⟨hp, x, hx⟩ := hq
  have hcolon :
    ((⊥ : Submodule S (S ⧸ I)).colon {x}) =
      Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) ((⊥ : Ideal (S ⧸ I)).colon {x}) := by
    apply le_antisymm
    · intro s hs
      rw [Submodule.mem_colon_singleton] at hs
      rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Submodule.mem_colon_singleton]
      have hsmul : s • x = (Ideal.Quotient.mk I s) * x := by
        rw [Algebra.smul_def]; rfl
      rw [hsmul] at hs
      simpa [Submodule.mem_bot] using hs
    · intro s hs
      rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Submodule.mem_colon_singleton] at hs
      rw [Submodule.mem_colon_singleton]
      have hsmul : s • x = (Ideal.Quotient.mk I s) * x := by
        rw [Algebra.smul_def]; rfl
      rw [hsmul]
      simpa [Submodule.mem_bot] using hs
  have hcomap :
    Ideal.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) (((⊥ : Ideal (S ⧸ I)).colon {x}).radical) = q := by
    rw [Ideal.comap_radical, ← hcolon, ← hx]
  refine ⟨((⊥ : Ideal (S ⧸ I)).colon {x}).radical, ⟨?_, x, rfl⟩, hcomap.symm⟩
  have hsurj := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (I := I)
  rw [← Ideal.map_comap_of_surjective _ hsurj (((⊥ : Ideal (S ⧸ I)).colon {x}).radical)]
  rw [hcomap]
  apply Ideal.map_isPrime_of_surjective hsurj
  rw [Ideal.mk_ker, hx]
  refine le_trans ?_ Ideal.le_radical
  rw [hcolon]
  intro s hs
  rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Submodule.mem_colon_singleton, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.mpr hs]
  simp

omit [IsNoetherianRing R] [p.IsPrime] in
/-- For an analytically unramified prime `p`, every associated prime of `R^ ⧸ p R^` is a
minimal prime over `p R^`: reducedness makes the associated primes minimal. -/
lemma l1_assoc_minimal (hunr : AnalyticallyUnramifiedPrime p) (q : Ideal (mCompletion R))
    (hq : IsAssociatedPrime q (mCompletion R ⧸ pCompletion p)) :
    q ∈ (pCompletion p).minimalPrimes := by
  -- `R^/pR^` is reduced (the hypothesis `hunr`).
  have : IsReduced (mCompletion R ⧸ pCompletion p) := hunr
  -- The associated prime `q` of the `R^`-module `R^/pR^` is the comap of an
  -- associated prime `q'` of the ring `R^/pR^` over itself.
  obtain ⟨q', hq', hcomap⟩ := exists_assoc_prime_quotient_comap hq
  -- In the reduced ring `R^/pR^`, `q'` is a minimal prime of `⊥`.
  have hmin : q' ∈ minimalPrimes (mCompletion R ⧸ pCompletion p) :=
    assoc_prime_mem_minimalPrimes_of_isReduced hq'
  -- Minimal primes over `pCompletion p` are exactly comaps of minimal primes
  -- of `⊥` in the quotient.
  rw [Ideal.minimalPrimes_eq_comap]
  exact ⟨q', hmin, hcomap.symm⟩

omit [IsNoetherianRing R] [p.IsPrime] in
/-- **L2 (maximal ideal of the localization).** If `q` is minimal over
`pCompletion p`, then the maximal ideal of `(R^)_q` is the extension of
`pCompletion p`, i.e. `(pCompletion p).map (algebraMap _ (Localization.AtPrime q))
= IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q)`.

*Argument.* The maximal ideal of `(R^)_q` is `q (R^)_q`. Since `q` is *minimal*
over `pCompletion p`, the radical of `pCompletion p · (R^)_q` is the maximal
ideal `q (R^)_q` (minimality says `q` is the only prime of `(R^)_q`, up to the
maximal ideal, lying over `pCompletion p`). Reducedness of `R^/pR^` localizes to
reducedness of `(R^)_q /pCompletion p (R^)_q`, which forces
`pCompletion p · (R^)_q` to already be radical, hence equal to its radical
`q (R^)_q = maximalIdeal`. -/
lemma l2_maximalIdeal_eq (q : Ideal (mCompletion R)) [q.IsPrime]
    (hunr : AnalyticallyUnramifiedPrime p) (hmin : q ∈ (pCompletion p).minimalPrimes) :
    (pCompletion p).map (algebraMap (mCompletion R) (Localization.AtPrime q)) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
  set S := mCompletion R
  set L := Localization.AtPrime q
  set f := algebraMap S L with hf
  set I := pCompletion p with hI
  set M := I.map f with hM
  -- L is a local ring
  have : IsLocalRing L := IsLocalization.AtPrime.isLocalRing L q
  -- maximal ideal of L is q.map f
  have hmaxq : q.map f = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L :=
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal q L
  -- Part 1: M.radical = maximalIdeal L
  have hrad : M.radical = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L := by
    rw [Ideal.radical_eq_sInf]
    have hset : {J : Ideal L | M ≤ J ∧ J.IsPrime} = {IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L} := by
      ext J
      simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_singleton_iff]
      constructor
      · rintro ⟨hMJ, hJprime⟩
        -- J' = comap f J is prime, ≤ q, and ⊇ I
        set J' := Ideal.under S J with hJ'
        have hJ'prime : J'.IsPrime :=
          ((IsLocalization.isPrime_iff_isPrime_disjoint q.primeCompl L J).mp hJprime).left
        have hdisj : Disjoint (q.primeCompl : Set S) (J' : Set S) :=
          ((IsLocalization.isPrime_iff_isPrime_disjoint q.primeCompl L J).mp hJprime).right
        -- J' ≤ q : from disjointness with primeCompl
        have hJ'q : J' ≤ q := by
          intro x hx
          by_contra hxq
          exact Set.disjoint_left.mp hdisj hxq hx
        -- minimality, applied to `I ≤ J'`: q ≤ J'
        have hJ'eq : J' = q :=
          le_antisymm hJ'q (hmin.right ⟨hJ'prime, Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp hMJ⟩ hJ'q)
        -- J = map f J' = map f q = maximalIdeal
        have hJmap : Ideal.map f J' = J := IsLocalization.map_under q.primeCompl L J
        rw [← hJmap, hJ'eq, hmaxq]
      · rintro rfl
        refine ⟨?_, (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal L).isPrime⟩
        rw [← hmaxq, hM]
        exact Ideal.map_mono hmin.left.right
    rw [hset, csInf_singleton]
  -- Part 2: M is radical, using reducedness
  have hredQ : IsReduced (S ⧸ I) := hunr
  have : IsLocalization (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (S ⧸ I) q.primeCompl) (L ⧸ M) :=
    IsLocalization.instQuotientIdealAlgebraMapSubmonoidMapRingHomAlgebraMap q.primeCompl L I
  have hredL : IsReduced (L ⧸ M) :=
    isReduced_localizationPreserves (Algebra.algebraMapSubmonoid (S ⧸ I) q.primeCompl) (L ⧸ M)
      hredQ
  have hMrad : M.IsRadical := (Ideal.isRadical_iff_quotient_reduced M).mpr hredL
  -- Combine
  rw [← hMrad.radical, hrad]

/-- If the maximal ideal of a Noetherian local ring is `(t)`, every nonzero element is a unit
times a power of `t` (by the Krull intersection theorem). -/
private lemma exists_unit_mul_pow_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] (t : A) (htgen : Ideal.span {t} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) (a : A)
    (ha : a ≠ 0) : ∃ (n : ℕ) (u : A), IsUnit u ∧ a = u * t ^ n := by
  classical
  have hmpow : ∀ n : ℕ, IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ^ n = Ideal.span {t ^ n} := by
    intro n
    rw [← htgen, Ideal.span_singleton_pow]
  have hkrull : ⨅ i, (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) ^ i = ⊥ :=
    Ideal.iInf_pow_eq_bot_of_isLocalRing _ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal A).ne_top
  have hN : ∃ N, a ∉ Ideal.span {t ^ N} := by
    by_contra h
    push Not at h
    apply ha
    have hmem : a ∈ ⨅ i, (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) ^ i := by
      rw [Submodule.mem_iInf]
      intro i
      rw [hmpow]; exact h i
    rw [hkrull] at hmem
    simpa using hmem
  -- Take the least such `N`; then `n = N - 1` is the order of `a`.
  have hNspec : a ∉ Ideal.span {t ^ (Nat.find hN)} := Nat.find_spec hN
  have hN0 : Nat.find hN ≠ 0 := by
    intro h
    apply hNspec
    rw [h, pow_zero, Ideal.span_singleton_one]
    trivial
  set n := Nat.find hN - 1 with hndef
  have hNeq : Nat.find hN = n + 1 := by omega
  rw [hNeq] at hNspec
  have hin : a ∈ Ideal.span {t ^ n} := by
    by_contra h
    have := Nat.find_min' hN h
    omega
  rw [Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hin
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hin
  -- The cofactor `c` is a unit: otherwise `c ∈ m = (t)` and `a ∈ (tⁿ⁺¹)`.
  have hcunit : IsUnit c := by
    rw [← IsLocalRing.notMem_maximalIdeal]
    intro hcm
    apply hNspec
    rw [← htgen, Ideal.mem_span_singleton] at hcm
    obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := hcm
    rw [Ideal.mem_span_singleton, hc, hd]
    exact ⟨d, by ring⟩
  exact ⟨n, c, hcunit, by rw [hc]; ring⟩

/-- **Krull-intersection regularity.** In a Noetherian local ring `A`, if the
maximal ideal is principal `= (t)` and `t` is not nilpotent, then `t` is a
nonzerodivisor.

*Argument.* `mⁿ = (tⁿ)`; Krull intersection gives `⋂ₙ mⁿ = ⊥`. If `t·y = 0` with
`y ≠ 0`, take the largest `n` with `y ∈ mⁿ = (tⁿ)`, write `y = tⁿ·c` with `c` a
unit (else `y ∈ (tⁿ⁺¹)`), and conclude `tⁿ⁺¹ = 0`, contradicting non-nilpotency. -/
@[sga "2 IV 5.3" "case n = 1"]
lemma regular_of_principal_maximalIdeal_of_not_nilpotent {A : Type*} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [IsNoetherianRing A] (t : A) (htgen : Ideal.span {t} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (htnn : ∀ n : ℕ, t ^ n ≠ 0) : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors A := by
  rw [mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff]
  have key : ∀ y : A, t * y = 0 → y = 0 := by
    intro y hy
    by_contra hyne
    obtain ⟨n, u, hu, rfl⟩ := exists_unit_mul_pow_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span t htgen y hyne
    have heq : t ^ (n + 1) * u = 0 := by rw [← hy]; ring
    exact htnn (n + 1) (hu.mul_left_eq_zero.mp heq)
  exact ⟨key, fun y hy => key y (by rwa [mul_comm])⟩

/- **L3 (uniformizer in `R`).** Since `R_p` is a DVR, `p R_p` is principal:
there exists `x ∈ R` whose image in `(R^)_q` generates the maximal ideal of
`(R^)_q`, and whose image `x̄` in `(R^)_q` is *not nilpotent*. (Non-nilpotency is
what we actually need downstream; via `regular_of_principal_maximalIdeal_of_not_nilpotent`
together with generation it yields that `x̄` is a nonzerodivisor in `(R^)_q`, and
that the maximal ideal is nonzero — WITHOUT requiring `x` to be a nonzerodivisor
in `R`, which is genuinely false in the presence of embedded associated primes
over `p`.)

*Argument (generation, A).* A DVR has principal maximal ideal; pick a uniformizer
`t` of `R_p` and a representative `x ∈ R` with `x/1 = (unit)·t`, so `x ∈ p` and
`x/1` generates `m_{R_p}`. For `a ∈ p`, write `a/1 = u·(x/1)` in `R_p`; clearing
denominators there is `s, w ∉ p` with `w(sa - bx) = 0` in `R`. Since `q ∩ R = p`
(going-down for the flat map `R → R^` + minimality of `q` over `pR^`), the images
of `s, w` are units in `(R^)_q`, whence `ā ∈ (x̄)`. As the maximal ideal of
`(R^)_q` is the image of `p` (= `hmax`), this gives `span {x̄} = maximalIdeal`.

*Argument (non-nilpotency, B).* `x̄ⁿ = algebraMap R (R^)_q (xⁿ)`. The image of
`x` in `R_p` is a uniformizer of the DVR `R_p`, so `(x/1)ⁿ ≠ 0` in `R_p` for all
`n`. The localization map `R_p → (R^)_q` (the base change of the flat `R → R^`
along `q ∩ R = p`) is faithfully flat, hence injective, so `x̄ⁿ ≠ 0`. (Mathlib
leads: `IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_irreducible`, going-down
`Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat`, `IsLocalization` base-change, faithful flatness
⇒ injective.) -/

/-- Helper for L3: the contraction of `q` to `R` is `p`, i.e. `q ∩ R = p`.

*Argument.* From `hmax`, `pCompletion p ≤ q` (pulling back the maximal ideal of
`(R^)_q`), so `p ≤ comap f q`. For the reverse inclusion we use going-down for
the flat map `R → R^` (`Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat`): if `p < comap f q` there
is a prime `P ≤ q` lying over `p`, hence `pCompletion p ≤ P`; minimality of `q`
over `pCompletion p` (read off from `hmax` via the prime correspondence in the
localization) forces `q ≤ P`, so `comap f q = comap f P = p`, a contradiction. -/
lemma l3_comap_eq (q : Ideal (mCompletion R)) [q.IsPrime]
    (hmax :
      (pCompletion p).map (algebraMap (mCompletion R) (Localization.AtPrime q)) =
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q)) :
    Ideal.comap (algebraMap R (mCompletion R)) q = p := by
  set f := algebraMap R (mCompletion R) with hf
  set g := algebraMap (mCompletion R) (Localization.AtPrime q) with hg
  have hunderq :
      Ideal.under (mCompletion R) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q)) = q :=
    IsLocalization.AtPrime.under_maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) q
  have hpq : pCompletion p ≤ q :=
    calc
      pCompletion p ≤ Ideal.comap g ((pCompletion p).map g) := Ideal.le_comap_map
      _ = Ideal.comap g (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q)) := by rw [hmax]
      _ = q := hunderq
  have hple : p ≤ Ideal.comap f q := Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mp hpq
  have hmin : ∀ (P : Ideal (mCompletion R)), P.IsPrime → P ≤ q → pCompletion p ≤ P → q ≤ P := by
    intro P hPp hPq hpP
    have hdisjP : Disjoint (q.primeCompl : Set (mCompletion R)) (P : Set (mCompletion R)) :=
      Set.disjoint_left.mpr fun x hx hxP => hx (hPq hxP)
    have hPgprime : (P.map g).IsPrime :=
      IsLocalization.isPrime_of_isPrime_disjoint q.primeCompl _ P hPp hdisjP
    have hle : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) ≤ P.map g := by
      rw [← hmax]
      exact Ideal.map_mono hpP
    have hPgmax : P.map g = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) :=
      ((IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal.isMaximal _).eq_of_le hPgprime.ne_top hle).symm
    have hunderP : Ideal.under (mCompletion R) (P.map g) = P :=
      IsLocalization.under_map_of_isPrime_disjoint q.primeCompl _ hPp hdisjP
    exact (show P = q by rw [← hunderP, hPgmax, hunderq]).ge
  refine le_antisymm ?_ hple
  by_contra hlt
  have hplt : p < Ideal.under R q := by
    rw [lt_iff_le_and_ne]
    refine ⟨hple, ?_⟩
    intro heq; apply hlt
    rw [show Ideal.comap f q = Ideal.under R q from rfl, ← heq]
  have : Algebra.HasGoingDown R (mCompletion R) := Algebra.HasGoingDown.of_flat
  obtain ⟨P, hPle, hPp, hlies⟩ :=
    Algebra.HasGoingDown.exists_ideal_le_liesOver_of_lt (R := R) (S := mCompletion R) (p := p) q
      hplt
  have hunderP : Ideal.under R P = p := hlies.over.symm
  have hpP : pCompletion p ≤ P := Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr hunderP.ge
  have hPeq : P = q := le_antisymm hPle (hmin P hPp hPle hpP)
  exact hplt.ne (by rw [← hPeq, hunderP])

omit [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] in
/-- Helper for L3: since `R_p` is a DVR, its (principal) maximal ideal is
generated by the image of some `x ∈ p`. -/
lemma l3_dvr_generator [IsDomain (Localization.AtPrime p)]
    (hdvr : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime p)) :
    ∃ x ∈ p,
      Ideal.span {algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime p) x} =
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime p) := by
  set Rp := Localization.AtPrime p with hRp
  set t := Submodule.IsPrincipal.generator (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp) with ht
  have htgen : Ideal.span {t} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp := Ideal.span_singleton_generator _
  obtain ⟨⟨a, s⟩, hmk⟩ := IsLocalization.mk'_surjective p.primeCompl t
  simp only at hmk
  have hsunit : IsUnit (IsLocalization.mk' Rp 1 s) := by
    have h := IsLocalization.mk'_spec' Rp 1 s
    rw [isUnit_iff_exists]
    refine ⟨algebraMap R Rp (s : R), ?_, ?_⟩
    · rw [mul_comm, h]; simp
    · rw [h]; simp
  have hspan : Ideal.span {algebraMap R Rp a} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp := by
    rw [← htgen, ← hmk, IsLocalization.mk'_eq_mul_mk'_one, mul_comm]
    exact (Ideal.span_singleton_mul_left_unit hsunit _).symm
  have hap : a ∈ p := by
    have hmem : algebraMap R Rp a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp := by
      rw [← hspan]; exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
    have hcomap : Ideal.under R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp) = p :=
      IsLocalization.AtPrime.under_maximalIdeal Rp p
    have : a ∈ Ideal.under R (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp) := hmem
    rwa [hcomap] at this
  exact ⟨a, hap, hspan⟩

/-- With `R_p` a discrete valuation ring, `p R^` becomes the maximal ideal of `(R^)_q`, and it
is generated by a single element pulled back from a uniformizer of `R_p`. -/
lemma l3_uniformizer [IsDomain (Localization.AtPrime p)]
    (hdvr : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime p)) (q : Ideal (mCompletion R))
    [q.IsPrime]
    (hmax :
      (pCompletion p).map (algebraMap (mCompletion R) (Localization.AtPrime q)) =
        IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q)) :
    ∃ x : R,
      (∀ n : ℕ, (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q) x) ^ n ≠ 0) ∧
        Ideal.span {algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q) x} =
          IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
  -- abbreviations
  set Rp := Localization.AtPrime p with hRp
  set L := Localization.AtPrime q with hL
  -- q ∩ R = p (key fact: going-down for the flat map R → R^ + minimality of q)
  have hcomap : Ideal.comap (algebraMap R (mCompletion R)) q = p := l3_comap_eq p q hmax
  -- p.primeCompl maps to units in L (because s ∉ p ⇒ f s ∉ q)
  have hunits : ∀ s : p.primeCompl, IsUnit (algebraMap R L (s : R)) := by
    intro s
    have hsp : (s : R) ∉ p := s.property
    have hfsq : algebraMap R (mCompletion R) (s : R) ∉ q := by
      intro hmem
      apply hsp
      have : (s : R) ∈ Ideal.comap (algebraMap R (mCompletion R)) q := hmem
      rwa [hcomap] at this
    have hmem' : algebraMap R (mCompletion R) (s : R) ∈ q.primeCompl := hfsq
    have hu :=
      IsLocalization.map_units L (⟨algebraMap R (mCompletion R) (s : R), hmem'⟩ : q.primeCompl)
    rw [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R (mCompletion R) L]
    exact hu
  -- φ : R_p → (R^)_q
  let φ : Rp →+* L := IsLocalization.lift (M := p.primeCompl) (g := algebraMap R L) hunits
  have hφeq : ∀ r : R, φ (algebraMap R Rp r) = algebraMap R L r := fun r =>
    IsLocalization.lift_eq hunits r
  let : Algebra Rp L := φ.toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower R Rp L := by
    apply IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq
    intro r
    change algebraMap R L r = φ (algebraMap R Rp r)
    rw [hφeq]
  have halg : algebraMap Rp L = φ := rfl
  -- the DVR generator x ∈ p
  obtain ⟨x, hxp, hxgenp⟩ := l3_dvr_generator p hdvr
  -- Flatness: L is flat over R (composite R → R^ → L), hence flat over R_p.
  have : Module.Flat R (mCompletion R) := inferInstance
  have : Module.Flat (mCompletion R) L := IsLocalization.flat L q.primeCompl
  have : Module.Flat R L := Module.Flat.trans R (mCompletion R) L
  have : Module.Flat Rp L :=
    (Module.flat_iff_of_isLocalization (R := R) Rp p.primeCompl L).mpr inferInstance
  -- GENERATION (A): span {algebraMap R L x} = maximalIdeal L.
  have hmaxL : Ideal.map (algebraMap R L) p = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L := by
    rw [← hmax]
    change Ideal.map (algebraMap R L) p = Ideal.map (algebraMap (mCompletion R) L) (pCompletion p)
    rw [pCompletion, Ideal.map_map]
    congr 1
  have hxgenL : Ideal.span {algebraMap R L x} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L := by
    have h1 : algebraMap R L x = φ (algebraMap R Rp x) := (hφeq x).symm
    rw [h1]
    rw [show Ideal.span {φ (algebraMap R Rp x)} = (Ideal.span {algebraMap R Rp x}).map φ by
        rw [Ideal.map_span]; simp]
    rw [hxgenp]
    have hmaxRp : Ideal.map (algebraMap R Rp) p = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp :=
      IsLocalization.AtPrime.map_eq_maximalIdeal p Rp
    rw [← hmaxRp, Ideal.map_map]
    rw [show φ.comp (algebraMap R Rp) = algebraMap R L from IsLocalization.lift_comp hunits]
    exact hmaxL
  -- φ is a local homomorphism (it sends maximalIdeal R_p into maximalIdeal L).
  have : IsLocalHom φ := by
    have hmap : Ideal.map φ (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp) ≤ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal L := by
      rw [← hxgenp, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton, Ideal.span_le, Set.singleton_subset_iff,
        SetLike.mem_coe, show φ (algebraMap R Rp x) = algebraMap R L x from hφeq x, ← hxgenL]
      exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
    exact (IsLocalRing.local_hom_TFAE φ).out 3 1 |>.mp hmap
  -- A flat local hom of local rings is faithfully flat, hence injective.
  have : Module.FaithfullyFlat Rp L := Module.FaithfullyFlat.of_flat_of_isLocalHom
  have hinj : Function.Injective (algebraMap Rp L) := FaithfulSMul.algebraMap_injective Rp L
  have hφinj : Function.Injective φ := by
    rw [← halg]; exact hinj
  -- NON-NILPOTENCY (B): (algebraMap R L x)^n = φ ((x/1)^n), and φ is injective,
  -- while (x/1)^n ≠ 0 in the domain R_p.
  refine ⟨x, ?_, hxgenL⟩
  intro n hn
  have hval : (algebraMap R L x) ^ n = φ ((algebraMap R Rp x) ^ n) := by rw [map_pow, hφeq]
  rw [hval] at hn
  have hz : (algebraMap R Rp x) ^ n = 0 := hφinj (by rw [hn, map_zero])
  have hxne : algebraMap R Rp x ≠ 0 := by
    intro h0
    have hbot : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal Rp = ⊥ := by
      rw [← hxgenp, h0, Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot.mpr rfl]
    have hfield : IsField Rp := (IsLocalRing.isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq).mpr hbot
    exact (IsDiscreteValuationRing.not_isField Rp) hfield
  exact (pow_ne_zero n hxne) hz

/-- **L4 (uniformizer is a nonzerodivisor in the localization).** The element `x`
from L3 maps to a nonzerodivisor in `(R^)_q`.

*Argument.* `x` is a nonzerodivisor in `R`. Since `R → R^` is flat
(`AdicCompletion` is flat over a Noetherian local ring), regular elements stay
regular: the image of `x` in `R^` is a nonzerodivisor
(`algebraMap_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_flat`), hence so is its image in the
localization `(R^)_q` (`IsLocalization.nonZeroDivisors_le_comap`). -/
lemma l4_nonzerodivisor [IsDomain (Localization.AtPrime p)] (q : Ideal (mCompletion R)) [q.IsPrime]
    (x : R) (hx : x ∈ nonZeroDivisors R) :
    algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q) x ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
  -- Step A: the image of `x` in `R^ = mCompletion R` is a nonzerodivisor.
  -- `R → R^` is flat (`AdicCompletion` is flat over a Noetherian ring), and
  -- flatness sends nonzerodivisors to nonzerodivisors.
  have hxc : algebraMap R (mCompletion R) x ∈ nonZeroDivisors (mCompletion R) :=
    algebraMap_mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_flat hx
  -- Step B: the image in the localization `(R^)_q` is a nonzerodivisor.
  -- `Localization.AtPrime q = IsLocalization q.primeCompl _`, and localization
  -- maps send nonzerodivisors of the base into nonzerodivisors.
  have hloc :
    algebraMap (mCompletion R) (Localization.AtPrime q) (algebraMap R (mCompletion R) x) ∈
      nonZeroDivisors (Localization.AtPrime q) :=
    IsLocalization.nonZeroDivisors_le_comap q.primeCompl (Localization.AtPrime q) hxc
  -- Compose: `algebraMap R (R^)_q` factors as `R → R^ → (R^)_q`.
  rwa [IsScalarTower.algebraMap_apply R (mCompletion R) (Localization.AtPrime q)]

/-- **L5 (assemble: the localization is a DVR).** A Noetherian local ring whose
maximal ideal is nonzero and generated by a single nonzerodivisor is a DVR (and
in particular a domain). Applied to `(R^)_q` with the uniformizer `x` from L3–L4
this gives the conclusion.

*Argument.* If the maximal ideal `m'` of a Noetherian local ring `A` is generated
by a single nonzerodivisor `t` and is nonzero, then `A` is a one-dimensional
regular local ring, hence a DVR; in particular `A` is a domain. (Mathlib:
`IsDiscreteValuationRing.ofHasUnitMulPow` / characterizations via principal
maximal ideal generated by a regular nonunit element, e.g.
`IsDiscreteValuationRing.tfae` or `DiscreteValuationRing.ofPrime`-style lemmas.)
The `IsDomain` instance is part of the DVR conclusion / follows from `A` being
reduced (localization of reduced `R^/pR^`-data) with a unique minimal prime. -/
@[ega "0 17.1.4" "partial",
  ega "II 7.1.6" "regular ⇒ DVR",
  ega "III 7.6.3" "Local implication",
  ega "IV 14.5.7" "more general",
  ega "IV 3.4.1" "(iii)",
  ega "IV 3.4.1.2" "Parenthetical in β",
  ega "IV 5.12.7" "special case"]
lemma l5_assemble (A : Type*) [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (t : A)
    (ht : t ∈ nonZeroDivisors A) (htgen : Ideal.span {t} = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A)
    (htne : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A ≠ ⊥) : ∃ _ : IsDomain A, IsDiscreteValuationRing A := by
  -- Every nonzero `a` is `u * t ^ n` with `u` a unit.
  have key : ∀ a : A, a ≠ 0 → ∃ (n : ℕ) (u : A), IsUnit u ∧ a = u * t ^ n :=
    fun a ha => exists_unit_mul_pow_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span t htgen a ha
  -- Powers of `t` are nonzerodivisors.
  have htpow : ∀ k : ℕ, t ^ k ∈ nonZeroDivisors A := fun k => Submonoid.pow_mem _ ht k
  -- `A` is nontrivial (its maximal ideal is nonzero).
  have : Nontrivial A :=
    (subsingleton_or_nontrivial A).resolve_left fun _ => htne (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  -- `A` has no zero divisors: `a b = (uv) t^(n+m)`, and `t^(n+m)` is regular.
  have : NoZeroDivisors A := by
    refine ⟨fun {a b} hab => ?_⟩
    by_contra h
    push Not at h
    obtain ⟨ha, hb⟩ := h
    obtain ⟨n, u, hu, rfl⟩ := key a ha
    obtain ⟨m, v, hv, rfl⟩ := key b hb
    have heq : (u * v) * t ^ (n + m) = 0 := by
      rw [← hab]; ring
    have huv : IsUnit (u * v) := hu.mul hv
    have ht0 : t ^ (n + m) = 0 := huv.mul_right_eq_zero.mp heq
    exact (nonZeroDivisors.ne_zero (htpow (n + m))) ht0
  have hdom : IsDomain A := IsDomain.mk
  -- Now `A` is a Noetherian local domain that is not a field with principal
  -- maximal ideal, hence a DVR via the standard TFAE characterization.
  have hprinc : Submodule.IsPrincipal (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) := ⟨t, htgen.symm⟩
  exact ⟨hdom, ((IsDiscreteValuationRing.TFAE A
    (IsLocalRing.isField_iff_maximalIdeal_eq.not.mpr htne)).out 5 1).mp hprinc⟩

end Sketch

/- **Completion of a Noetherian local ring is Noetherian** (Stacks Tag 0316,
restricted to the `m`-adic completion of a Noetherian local ring). This is the
analytic kernel underlying `hNoeth` in
`exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_atPrime_of_analyticallyUnramified`.

*Proof sketch.* Since `R` is Noetherian, its maximal
ideal `m = (f₁,…,fₙ)` is finitely generated. There is a surjective ring
homomorphism `Φ : R[[X₁,…,Xₙ]] = MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R → R^` sending `Xᵢ ↦ fᵢ`
(built from the compatible family of "truncated evaluation mod `mᵏ`" maps
`Φₖ : A → R/mᵏ`, using `AdicCompletion`'s description as compatible families). The
multivariate power-series ring `A` is Noetherian (iterated single-variable
`PowerSeries.instIsNoetherianRing` across the reindexing iso
`MvPowerSeries (Fin (n+1)) R ≃+* PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R)`). A
surjective image of a Noetherian ring is Noetherian
(`isNoetherianRing_of_surjective`). -/

namespace Stacks.NoetherianCompletion

open MvPowerSeries
variable {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {n : ℕ}

/-- For each `k`, the family `i ↦ (f i mod m^k)` admits evaluation of power series, when
`R ⧸ m^k` is given the discrete (`⊥`) uniformity: each `f i ∈ m` is nilpotent mod `m^k`
(hence topologically nilpotent), and `Fin n` is finite so the cofinite filter is `⊥`. -/
theorem hev_aux (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) (k : ℕ) :
    letI : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⊥
    MvPowerSeries.HasEval (fun i => (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) (f i)) := by
  let : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⊥
  have : DiscreteTopology (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⟨rfl⟩
  refine ⟨fun s => IsNilpotent.isTopologicallyNilpotent ⟨k, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
  · rw [← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact Ideal.pow_mem_pow (hf s) k
  · rw [Filter.cofinite_eq_bot]
    exact Filter.tendsto_bot

/-- The truncated evaluation ring hom `Φ_k : R[[X_1,…,X_n]] →+* R ⧸ m^k`, sending `X_i ↦ f̄_i`
and a constant `c ↦ c̄`. Built as `MvPowerSeries.eval₂Hom` for the discrete topology on `R ⧸ m^k`
(only finitely many monomials survive since `f̄_i` is nilpotent). -/
noncomputable def Φk (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) (k : ℕ) :
    MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R →+* R ⧸ m ^ k := by
  letI : UniformSpace R := ⊥
  letI : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⊥
  exact
    MvPowerSeries.eval₂Hom (φ := Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) (a := fun i =>
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) (f i)) continuous_of_discreteTopology (hev_aux m f hf k)

/-- The underlying function of `Φk` is `MvPowerSeries.eval₂` at the reduced generators. -/
theorem Φk_coe (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) (k : ℕ) :
    letI : UniformSpace R := ⊥
    letI : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⊥
    ⇑(Φk m f hf k) =
      MvPowerSeries.eval₂ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k))
        (fun i => (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) (f i)) := by
  let : UniformSpace R := ⊥
  let : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⊥
  rw [Φk, MvPowerSeries.coe_eval₂Hom]

/-- The family `(Φ_k)` is compatible with the transition maps `R ⧸ m^b → R ⧸ m^a` (`a ≤ b`):
"evaluate, then reduce" equals "reduce, then evaluate". Proved via `MvPowerSeries.comp_eval₂`
and `Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk`. -/
theorem Φk_compat (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) {a b : ℕ} (h : a ≤ b) :
    (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h).comp (Φk m f hf b) = Φk m f hf a := by
  let : UniformSpace R := ⊥
  let : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ a) := ⊥
  let : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ b) := ⊥
  have : DiscreteTopology (R ⧸ m ^ b) := ⟨rfl⟩
  apply RingHom.ext
  intro x
  change (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h) (Φk m f hf b x) = Φk m f hf a x
  have hcompeq :=
    MvPowerSeries.comp_eval₂ (φ := (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ b))) (a := fun i =>
      (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ b)) (f i)) (continuous_of_discreteTopology) (hev_aux m f hf b) (ε :=
      (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h)) (continuous_of_discreteTopology)
  have key :
    (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h) (Φk m f hf b x) =
      MvPowerSeries.eval₂ ((Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ b)))
        (fun i => (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h) ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ b)) (f i))) x := by
    rw [Φk_coe]; exact congrFun hcompeq x
  rw [key]
  have e1 :
    (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ b)) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ a) := by
    apply RingHom.ext; intro y; rw [RingHom.comp_apply]; exact Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk _ y
  have e2 :
    (fun i => (Ideal.Quotient.factorPow m h) ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ b)) (f i))) =
      (fun i => (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ a)) (f i)) := by
    funext i; exact Ideal.Quotient.factor_mk _ (f i)
  rw [e1, e2, ← Φk_coe]

/-- The assembled ring hom `Φ : R[[X_1,…,X_n]] →+* R^` (Part A of the argument), obtained
from the compatible family `(Φ_k)` by the universal property `AdicCompletion.liftRingHom`. -/
noncomputable def Φ (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) :
    MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R →+* AdicCompletion m R :=
  AdicCompletion.liftRingHom m (fun k => Φk m f hf k) (fun {_ _} h => Φk_compat m f hf h)

/-- The truncations of `Φ` are the maps `Φk`: evaluating `Φ` modulo `m ^ k` gives `Φk` at `k`. -/
theorem evalₐ_Φ (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) (k : ℕ)
    (x : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R) : (AdicCompletion.evalₐ m k) (Φ m f hf x) = Φk m f hf k x := by
  rw [Φ]; exact AdicCompletion.evalₐ_liftRingHom m _ _ k x

/-- Antidiagonal reindexing identity underlying `map_mul` of the sum/curry isomorphism:
the antidiagonal of `e.symm (s,t)` maps bijectively to `antidiagonal s ×ˢ antidiagonal t`. -/
theorem mvps_bij_sum (σ τ A : Type*) [CommRing A] [DecidableEq σ] [DecidableEq τ]
    (φ ψ : MvPowerSeries (σ ⊕ τ) A) (e : (σ ⊕ τ →₀ ℕ) ≃+ (σ →₀ ℕ) × (τ →₀ ℕ)) (s : σ →₀ ℕ)
    (t : τ →₀ ℕ) :
    (∑ p ∈ Finset.antidiagonal (e.symm (s, t)), φ p.1 * ψ p.2) =
      ∑ x ∈ (Finset.antidiagonal s) ×ˢ (Finset.antidiagonal t),
        φ (e.symm (x.1.1, x.2.1)) * ψ (e.symm (x.1.2, x.2.2)) := by
  apply
    Finset.sum_nbij' (i := fun p =>
      (((e p.fst).fst, (e p.snd).fst), ((e p.fst).snd, (e p.snd).snd))) (j := fun x =>
      (e.symm (x.fst.fst, x.snd.fst), e.symm (x.fst.snd, x.snd.snd)))
  · intro a ha
    rw [Finset.mem_antidiagonal] at ha
    rw [Finset.mem_product, Finset.mem_antidiagonal, Finset.mem_antidiagonal]
    have h2 : e a.fst + e a.snd = (s, t) := by
      rw [← map_add, ha]; exact e.apply_symm_apply _
    exact
      ⟨by
        have := congrArg Prod.fst h2; simpa using this, by
        have := congrArg Prod.snd h2; simpa using this⟩
  · intro x hx
    rw [Finset.mem_product, Finset.mem_antidiagonal, Finset.mem_antidiagonal] at hx
    rw [Finset.mem_antidiagonal]
    have :
      e.symm (x.fst.fst, x.snd.fst) + e.symm (x.fst.snd, x.snd.snd) =
        e.symm ((x.fst.fst + x.fst.snd), (x.snd.fst + x.snd.snd)) := by
      rw [← map_add]; rfl
    rw [this, hx.left, hx.right]
  · intro a ha
    have ea1 : e.symm ((e a.fst).fst, (e a.fst).snd) = a.fst := by
      rw [Prod.mk.eta]; exact e.symm_apply_apply _
    have ea2 : e.symm ((e a.snd).fst, (e a.snd).snd) = a.snd := by
      rw [Prod.mk.eta]; exact e.symm_apply_apply _
    simp only [Prod.mk.eta]; rw [ea1, ea2]
  · intro x hx
    rw [e.apply_symm_apply, e.apply_symm_apply]
  · intro a ha
    simp only
    have ea1 : e.symm ((e a.fst).fst, (e a.fst).snd) = a.fst := by
      rw [Prod.mk.eta]; exact e.symm_apply_apply _
    have ea2 : e.symm ((e a.snd).fst, (e a.snd).snd) = a.snd := by
      rw [Prod.mk.eta]; exact e.symm_apply_apply _
    rw [ea1, ea2]

/-- Sum/curry ring isomorphism `MvPowerSeries (σ ⊕ τ) A ≃+* MvPowerSeries σ (MvPowerSeries τ A)`,
hand-built since it is missing from Mathlib. -/
noncomputable def mvps_sumCurry (σ τ A : Type*) [CommRing A] :
    MvPowerSeries (σ ⊕ τ) A ≃+* MvPowerSeries σ (MvPowerSeries τ A)
    where
  toFun φ := fun s => fun t => φ (Finsupp.sumFinsuppAddEquivProdFinsupp.symm (s, t))
  invFun ψ := fun n =>
    ψ (Finsupp.sumFinsuppAddEquivProdFinsupp n).fst (Finsupp.sumFinsuppAddEquivProdFinsupp n).snd
  left_inv := by
    intro φ; funext n; simp
  right_inv := by
    intro ψ; funext s t; simp
  map_add' := by
    intro φ ψ; rfl
  map_mul' := by
    classical
    intro φ ψ
    set e := @Finsupp.sumFinsuppAddEquivProdFinsupp ℕ _ σ τ with he
    apply MvPowerSeries.ext
    intro s
    apply MvPowerSeries.ext
    intro t
    set Fφ : MvPowerSeries σ (MvPowerSeries τ A) := fun s => fun t => φ (e.symm (s, t)) with hFφ
    set Fψ : MvPowerSeries σ (MvPowerSeries τ A) := fun s => fun t => ψ (e.symm (s, t)) with hFψ
    have hRouter :
      (MvPowerSeries.coeff s) (Fφ * Fψ) =
        ∑ p ∈ Finset.antidiagonal s,
          (MvPowerSeries.coeff p.fst Fφ) * (MvPowerSeries.coeff p.snd Fψ) :=
      MvPowerSeries.coeff_mul s Fφ Fψ
    have hInner :
      ∀ p : (σ →₀ ℕ) × (σ →₀ ℕ),
        (MvPowerSeries.coeff t) ((MvPowerSeries.coeff p.fst Fφ) * (MvPowerSeries.coeff p.snd Fψ)) =
          ∑ q ∈ Finset.antidiagonal t, φ (e.symm (p.fst, q.fst)) * ψ (e.symm (p.snd, q.snd)) := by
      intro p
      rw [@MvPowerSeries.coeff_mul τ A _ t _ _ (Classical.decEq τ)]; rfl
    trans (∑ p ∈ Finset.antidiagonal (e.symm (s, t)), φ p.fst * ψ p.snd)
    · change (MvPowerSeries.coeff (e.symm (s, t))) (φ * ψ) = _
      rw [MvPowerSeries.coeff_mul]; rfl
    · symm
      change (MvPowerSeries.coeff t) ((MvPowerSeries.coeff s) (Fφ * Fψ)) = _
      rw [hRouter, map_sum]
      rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun p _ => hInner p)]
      rw [← Finset.sum_product']
      exact (mvps_bij_sum σ τ A φ ψ e s t).symm

/-- Empty-index power-series ring is just the base ring. -/
noncomputable def mvps_emptyEquiv (σ A : Type*) [CommRing A] [IsEmpty σ] :
    MvPowerSeries σ A ≃+* A :=
  RingEquiv.ofRingHom (MvPowerSeries.constantCoeff (σ := σ) (R := A))
    (MvPowerSeries.C (σ := σ) (R := A))
    (by
      ext r; simp)
    (by
      classical
      ext φ n
      have hn : n = 0 := Subsingleton.elim _ _
      subst hn
      simp [MvPowerSeries.coeff_C, MvPowerSeries.coeff_zero_eq_constantCoeff])

/-- The single-step reindexing isomorphism for the induction. -/
noncomputable def mvps_stepEquiv (m : ℕ) (A : Type*) [CommRing A] :
    MvPowerSeries (Fin (m + 1)) A ≃+* PowerSeries (MvPowerSeries (Fin m) A) :=
  let eFin : Fin (m + 1) ≃ Unit ⊕ Fin m :=
    (finCongr (by omega : m + 1 = 1 + m)).trans
      (finSumFinEquiv.symm.trans (finOneEquiv.sumCongr (Equiv.refl (Fin m))))
  ((MvPowerSeries.renameEquiv A eFin).toRingEquiv).trans (mvps_sumCurry Unit (Fin m) A)

/-- Total degree of a multi-index. -/
noncomputable def mdeg (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) : ℕ :=
  d.sum fun _ e => e

/-- The total degree of a multi-index is the sum of its exponents. -/
theorem mdeg_eq_sum (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) : mdeg d = ∑ i, d i :=
  Finsupp.sum_fintype d (fun _ e => e) (fun _ => rfl)

/-- `f^d ∈ m ^ (mdeg d)`. -/
theorem fpow_mem (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) :
    (d.prod fun s e => (f s) ^ e) ∈ m ^ (mdeg d) := by
  rw [Finsupp.prod_pow, mdeg_eq_sum, ← Finset.prod_pow_eq_pow_sum]
  exact Ideal.prod_mem_prod (fun i _ => Ideal.pow_mem_pow (hf i) _)

/-- There are finitely many functions `Fin n → ℕ` bounded by `k`. -/
theorem finite_fun_lt (k : ℕ) : Set.Finite {g : Fin n → ℕ | ∀ i, g i < k} := by
  have h : {g : Fin n → ℕ | ∀ i, g i < k} = Set.univ.pi (fun _ : Fin n => Set.Iio k) := by
    ext g; simp [Set.mem_pi]
  rw [h]; exact Set.Finite.pi (fun _ => Set.finite_Iio k)

/-- There are finitely many multi-indices all of whose exponents are `< k`. -/
theorem finite_lt (k : ℕ) : Set.Finite {d : Fin n →₀ ℕ | ∀ i, d i < k} := by
  apply Set.Finite.subset ((finite_fun_lt k).image (Finsupp.equivFunOnFinite.symm))
  intro d hd
  refine ⟨(d : Fin n → ℕ), hd, ?_⟩
  ext i; simp

/-- There are finitely many multi-indices of total degree `< k`. -/
theorem finite_mdeg_lt (k : ℕ) : Set.Finite {d : Fin n →₀ ℕ | mdeg d < k} := by
  apply Set.Finite.subset (finite_lt k)
  intro d hd i
  simp only [Set.mem_ofPred_eq] at hd ⊢
  calc
    d i ≤ mdeg d := by
      rw [mdeg_eq_sum]
      exact Finset.single_le_sum (fun _ _ => Nat.zero_le _) (Finset.mem_univ i)
    _ < k := hd

/-- The finite set of multi-indices of total degree `< k`. -/
noncomputable def monFinset (k : ℕ) : Finset (Fin n →₀ ℕ) :=
  (finite_mdeg_lt (n := n) k).toFinset

/-- Membership in `monFinset k` is having total degree `< k`. -/
theorem mem_monFinset {k : ℕ} {d : Fin n →₀ ℕ} : d ∈ monFinset k ↔ mdeg d < k := by
  rw [monFinset, Set.Finite.mem_toFinset]; rfl

/-- The monomial `f^d = ∏ i, (f i)^(d i)`. -/
noncomputable def fmon (f : Fin n → R) (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) : R :=
  d.prod fun s e => (f s) ^ e

/-- The set of monomials `f^d` of total degree `k`. -/
def fmonSet (f : Fin n → R) (k : ℕ) : Set R :=
  {x : R | ∃ d : Fin n →₀ ℕ, mdeg d = k ∧ x = fmon f d}

/-- `fmonSet f k` is the image of the degree-`k` multi-indices under `d ↦ f ^ d`. -/
theorem fmonSet_eq_image (f : Fin n → R) (k : ℕ) :
    fmonSet f k = (fmon f) '' {d : Fin n →₀ ℕ | mdeg d = k} := by
  ext x
  simp only [fmonSet, Set.mem_ofPred_eq, Set.mem_image]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩; exact ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩
  · rintro ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩; exact ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩

/-- Bumping one exponent raises the total degree by one. -/
theorem mdeg_add_single (i : Fin n) (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) :
    mdeg (d + Finsupp.single i 1) = mdeg d + 1 := by
  rw [mdeg_eq_sum, mdeg_eq_sum]; simp [Finset.sum_add_distrib]

/-- Multiplying the monomial `f ^ d` by `f i` bumps the `i`-th exponent. -/
theorem fmul (f : Fin n → R) (i : Fin n) (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) :
    f i * fmon f d = fmon f (d + Finsupp.single i 1) := by
  rw [fmon, fmon,
    Finsupp.prod_add_index
      (by
        intro a _; simp)
      (by
        intro a _ b₁ b₂; rw [pow_add])]
  rw [Finsupp.prod_single_index (by simp)]; ring

open Pointwise in
/-- `m ^ k` is contained in the `R`-span of the degree-`k` monomials `f ^ d`, where
`m = span (range f)`. -/
theorem mpow_le_span (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m) (k : ℕ) :
    m ^ k ≤ Ideal.span (fmonSet f k) := by
  induction k with
  | zero =>
    rw [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top, top_le_iff, Ideal.eq_top_iff_one]
    exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨0, by simp [mdeg], by simp [fmon]⟩
  | succ k ih =>
    rw [pow_succ]
    have h1 : m ^ k * m ≤ Ideal.span (fmonSet f k) * Ideal.span (Set.range f) := by
      rw [hspan]; exact Ideal.mul_mono ih le_rfl
    refine h1.trans ?_
    rw [Ideal.span_mul_span]
    apply Ideal.span_mono
    rintro x ⟨a, ⟨d, hd, rfl⟩, b, ⟨i, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨d + Finsupp.single i 1, by rw [mdeg_add_single, hd], ?_⟩
    change fmon f d * f i = _
    rw [mul_comm]; exact fmul f i d

/-- **Lemma 1 (representation form).** Every `r ∈ m^k` is a finite `R`-combination of degree-`k`
monomials `f^d`. -/
theorem mpow_repr (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m) (k : ℕ)
    (r : R) (hr : r ∈ m ^ k) :
    ∃ l : (Fin n →₀ ℕ) →₀ R,
      (∀ d ∈ l.support, mdeg d = k) ∧ (l.sum fun d a => a * fmon f d) = r := by
  have hmem : r ∈ Ideal.span (fmonSet f k) := mpow_le_span m f hspan k hr
  rw [show Ideal.span (fmonSet f k) = Submodule.span R (fmonSet f k) from rfl, fmonSet_eq_image,
    Finsupp.mem_span_image_iff_linearCombination] at hmem
  obtain ⟨l, hlsupp, hlc⟩ := hmem
  rw [Finsupp.mem_supported] at hlsupp
  refine ⟨l, fun d hd => hlsupp hd, ?_⟩
  rw [Finsupp.linearCombination_apply] at hlc
  rw [← hlc]
  exact Finsupp.sum_congr (fun d _ => by rw [smul_eq_mul])

/-- `Φ_k g` is the image, modulo `m ^ k`, of the finite sum `∑_{deg d < k} (coeff d g) · f ^ d`. -/
theorem Φk_eq_sum (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m) (k : ℕ)
    (g : MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R) :
    Φk m f hf k g = (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) (∑ d ∈ monFinset k, (coeff d) g * fmon f d) := by
  let : UniformSpace R := ⊥
  let : UniformSpace (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⊥
  have : DiscreteTopology (R ⧸ m ^ k) := ⟨rfl⟩
  have : DiscreteTopology R := ⟨rfl⟩
  have hterm : ∀ d : Fin n →₀ ℕ,
      ((Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) ((coeff d) g) *
          d.prod fun s e => (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) (f s) ^ e) =
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) ((coeff d) g * fmon f d) := by
    intro d
    rw [map_mul]
    congr 1
    rw [fmon, Finsupp.prod, Finsupp.prod, map_prod]
    exact Finset.prod_congr rfl fun i _ => by rw [map_pow]
  rw [show
      Φk m f hf k g =
        MvPowerSeries.eval₂ (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k))
          (fun i => (Ideal.Quotient.mk (m ^ k)) (f i)) g
      from congrFun (Φk_coe m f hf k) g,
    MvPowerSeries.eval₂_eq_tsum continuous_of_discreteTopology (hev_aux m f hf k) g, map_sum,
    tsum_eq_sum (s := monFinset k) ?_]
  · exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun d _ => hterm d
  · intro d hd
    rw [mem_monFinset] at hd
    rw [hterm d, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.pow_le_pow_right (not_lt.mp hd) (fpow_mem m f hf d))

open Classical in
/-- Choice of degree-`k` monomial coefficients lifting `r ∈ m^k`; `0` otherwise (total version). -/
noncomputable def liftDeg (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m)
    (k : ℕ) (r : R) : (Fin n →₀ ℕ) →₀ R :=
  if h : r ∈ m ^ k then (mpow_repr m f hspan k r h).choose else 0

/-- For `r ∈ m ^ k`, the coefficients `liftDeg … k r` are supported in total degree `k` and
represent `r` as a combination of degree-`k` monomials. -/
theorem liftDeg_spec (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m) (k : ℕ)
    (r : R) (hr : r ∈ m ^ k) :
    (∀ d ∈ (liftDeg m f hspan k r).support, mdeg d = k) ∧
      ((liftDeg m f hspan k r).sum fun d a => a * fmon f d) = r := by
  rw [liftDeg, dite_eq_left hr]; exact (mpow_repr m f hspan k r hr).choose_spec

/-- `liftDeg … k r` is supported in total degree exactly `k`. -/
theorem liftDeg_support (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m)
    (k : ℕ) (r : R) : ∀ d ∈ (liftDeg m f hspan k r).support, mdeg d = k := by
  intro d hd; rw [liftDeg] at hd; split at hd
  · rename_i hr; exact (mpow_repr m f hspan k r hr).choose_spec.left d hd
  · simp at hd

/-- `liftDeg … k r` vanishes on multi-indices of total degree different from `k`. -/
theorem liftDeg_apply_eq_zero (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m)
    (k : ℕ) (r : R) (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) (hne : mdeg d ≠ k) : (liftDeg m f hspan k r) d = 0 := by
  by_contra h
  exact hne (liftDeg_support m f hspan k r d (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.mpr h))

/-- The accumulated polynomial of degree `≤ k`: at each level `k` we add degree-`k` coefficients
chosen so that the truncated evaluation matches the Cauchy representative `a (k+1)`. -/
noncomputable def Gpoly (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m)
    (a : ℕ → R) : ℕ → ((Fin n →₀ ℕ) →₀ R)
  | 0 => liftDeg m f hspan 0 (a 1)
  | (k + 1) =>
    Gpoly m f hspan a k +
      liftDeg m f hspan (k + 1) (a (k + 2) - ((Gpoly m f hspan a k).sum fun d c => c * fmon f d))

/-- The accumulated polynomial of degree `≤ k` evaluates to the Cauchy representative
`a (k+1)`. -/
theorem Gpoly_inv (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m) (a : ℕ → R)
    (hcauchy : ∀ k, a (k + 1) - a k ∈ m ^ k) (k : ℕ) :
    ((Gpoly m f hspan a k).sum fun d c => c * fmon f d) = a (k + 1) := by
  induction k with
  | zero =>
    change ((liftDeg m f hspan 0 (a 1)).sum fun d c => c * fmon f d) = a 1
    have h1 : a 1 ∈ m ^ 0 := by
      rw [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]; exact Submodule.mem_top
    exact (liftDeg_spec m f hspan 0 (a 1) h1).right
  | succ k
    ih =>
    change
      ((Gpoly m f hspan a k +
              liftDeg m f hspan (k + 1)
                (a (k + 2) - ((Gpoly m f hspan a k).sum fun d c => c * fmon f d))).sum
          fun d c => c * fmon f d) =
        a (k + 2)
    rw [Finsupp.sum_add_index' (fun _ => zero_mul _) (fun _ _ _ => add_mul _ _ _), ih,
      (liftDeg_spec m f hspan (k + 1) (a (k + 2) - a (k + 1)) (hcauchy (k + 1))).right]
    ring

/-- `Gpoly … k` is supported in total degree at most `k`. -/
theorem Gpoly_support (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m)
    (a : ℕ → R) (k : ℕ) : ∀ d ∈ (Gpoly m f hspan a k).support, mdeg d ≤ k := by
  induction k with
  | zero =>
    intro d hd
    have := liftDeg_support m f hspan 0 (a 1) d hd; omega
  | succ k ih =>
    intro d hd
    have hsub :
      (Gpoly m f hspan a (k + 1)).support ⊆
        (Gpoly m f hspan a k).support ∪
          (liftDeg m f hspan (k + 1)
              (a (k + 2) - ((Gpoly m f hspan a k).sum fun d c => c * fmon f d))).support :=
      Finsupp.support_add
    rcases Finset.mem_union.mp (hsub hd) with h | h
    · exact le_trans (ih d h) (Nat.le_succ k)
    · rw [liftDeg_support m f hspan (k + 1) _ d h]

/-- The coefficient of a fixed multi-index `d` stabilizes once `k` reaches `mdeg d`. -/
theorem Gpoly_stable (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m)
    (a : ℕ → R) (d : Fin n →₀ ℕ) :
    ∀ k, mdeg d ≤ k → (Gpoly m f hspan a k) d = (Gpoly m f hspan a (mdeg d)) d := by
  intro k
  induction k with
  | zero =>
    intro h; have : mdeg d = 0 := by omega
    rw [this]
  | succ k ih =>
    intro h
    rcases Nat.lt_or_ge (mdeg d) (k + 1) with hlt | hge
    · change (Gpoly m f hspan a k + _) d = _
      rw [Finsupp.add_apply, liftDeg_apply_eq_zero m f hspan (k + 1) _ d (by omega), add_zero]
      exact ih (by omega)
    · have : mdeg d = k + 1 := by omega
      rw [this]

/-- The final coefficient/sum match: `∑_{deg d < k+1} (Gpoly _ (mdeg d)) d · f^d` equals the
`(Gpoly _ k)`-sum. -/
theorem Gpoly_sum_eq (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m)
    (a : ℕ → R) (k : ℕ) :
    (∑ d ∈ monFinset (k + 1), (Gpoly m f hspan a (mdeg d)) d * fmon f d) =
      ((Gpoly m f hspan a k).sum fun d c => c * fmon f d) := by
  rw [Finsupp.sum]
  have hcong :
    ∀ d ∈ monFinset (k + 1),
      (Gpoly m f hspan a (mdeg d)) d * fmon f d = (Gpoly m f hspan a k) d * fmon f d := by
    intro d hd
    rw [mem_monFinset] at hd
    rw [← Gpoly_stable m f hspan a d k (by omega)]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl hcong]
  symm
  apply Finset.sum_subset
  · intro d hd
    rw [mem_monFinset]
    exact Nat.lt_succ_of_le (Gpoly_support m f hspan a k d hd)
  · intro d _ hdnot
    rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff] at hdnot
    rw [hdnot, zero_mul]

-- needed: `Φ_surjective`'s `rw` only finds its pattern when isDefEq ignores transparency
-- (the completion is a semireducible definition that must unfold here).
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false in
/-- **Part B.** When `m = (f_0,…,f_{n-1})`, the evaluation map `Φ` is
surjective.

PROOF PLAN (not yet formalized): every `u : R^` is `AdicCompletion.mk a` for an adic Cauchy
sequence `a` (`AdicCompletion.mk_surjective`), so it suffices to find `g` with
`Φk k g = (a k mod m^k)` for all `k` (`AdicCompletion.ext_evalₐ`, `evalₐ_Φ`, `evalₐ_mk`). Build the
coefficients `c_α ∈ R` of `g` by induction on `|α|`, using Lemma 1 (`m^k = (f)^k` is spanned by the
degree-`k` monomials `f^α`, `|α| = k`, since `Ideal.span (range f) = m`) to absorb the discrepancy
`a_{d+1} - (∑_{|α|≤d} c_α f^α)` at each stage. -/
theorem Φ_surjective (m : Ideal R) (f : Fin n → R) (hf : ∀ i, f i ∈ m)
    (hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m) : Function.Surjective (Φ m f hf) := by
  -- completion; true for any CommRing given hspan; no counterexample)
  intro u
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := AdicCompletion.mk_surjective m R u
  -- The Cauchy sequence's consecutive differences lie in the appropriate powers of `m`.
  have hcauchy : ∀ k, (a : ℕ → R) (k + 1) - (a : ℕ → R) k ∈ m ^ k := by
    intro k
    have h := a.property (Nat.le_succ k)
    rw [SModEq.sub_mem] at h
    have he : (m ^ k) • (⊤ : Submodule R R) = m ^ k := by
      rw [Ideal.smul_top_eq_map]; simp
    rw [he] at h
    have h2 := neg_mem h
    rwa [neg_sub] at h2
  -- The witness power series: coefficient at `d` is read off `Gpoly` at level `mdeg d`.
  refine ⟨fun d => (Gpoly m f hspan (a : ℕ → R) (mdeg d)) d, ?_⟩
  apply AdicCompletion.ext_evalₐ
  intro k
  rw [evalₐ_Φ, AdicCompletion.evalₐ_mk, Φk_eq_sum]
  cases k with
  | zero =>
    have : Subsingleton (R ⧸ m ^ 0) := by
      rw [pow_zero, Ideal.one_eq_top]
      exact Ideal.Quotient.subsingleton_iff.mpr rfl
    exact Subsingleton.elim _ _
  | succ j =>
    congr 1
    change
      (∑ d ∈ monFinset (j + 1), (Gpoly m f hspan (a : ℕ → R) (mdeg d)) d * fmon f d) =
        (a : ℕ → R) (j + 1)
    rw [Gpoly_sum_eq, Gpoly_inv m f hspan (a : ℕ → R) hcauchy j]

end Stacks.NoetherianCompletion

/-- The `m`-adic completion of a Noetherian local ring is Noetherian: it is a surjective image
of the power-series ring in a finite generating set of `m`. -/
@[ega "0 7.3.1" "special case",
  ega "0 7.6.11" "(ii), special case",
  ega "I 10.6.4" "special case",
  ega "IV 8.11.4" "Â is Noetherian",
  sga "3 VIIB 5.5.2" "Noetherianity of Â",
  sga "3 X 4.0" "partial"]
lemma mCompletion_isNoetherianRing {R : Type*} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] :
    IsNoetherianRing (mCompletion R) := by
  -- standard true theorem, no counterexample)
  -- Extract finitely many generators of the (finitely generated) maximal ideal as a `Fin`-family.
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ := (isNoetherian_def.mp (inferInstance) (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R))
  set m := IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal R with hm
  have hgen : ∃ (n : ℕ) (f : Fin n → R), Ideal.span (Set.range f) = m ∧ ∀ i, f i ∈ m := by
    refine ⟨s.card, fun i => (s.equivFin.symm i : R), ?_, ?_⟩
    · have hrange : Set.range (fun i => ((s.equivFin.symm i : R))) = (s : Set R) := by
        ext x
        simp only [Set.mem_range, Finset.mem_coe]
        exact ⟨by rintro ⟨i, rfl⟩; exact (s.equivFin.symm i).property,
          fun hx => ⟨s.equivFin ⟨x, hx⟩, by simp⟩⟩
      rw [Ideal.span, hrange]
      exact hs
    · intro i
      rw [← hs]
      exact Submodule.subset_span (s.equivFin.symm i).property
  obtain ⟨n, f, hspan, hf⟩ := hgen
  -- `R[[X_1,…,X_n]]` is Noetherian (Part C), and `Φ` is a surjection onto `R^` (Parts A–B),
  -- so `R^` is Noetherian as a surjective image of a Noetherian ring.
  have : IsNoetherianRing (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R) :=
    mvPowerSeries_fin_isNoetherianRing R n
  exact
    isNoetherianRing_of_surjective (MvPowerSeries (Fin n) R) (mCompletion R)
      (Stacks.NoetherianCompletion.Φ m f hf)
      (Stacks.NoetherianCompletion.Φ_surjective m f hf hspan)

/-- **Stacks Tag 032Z.** Let `R` be a Noetherian local ring and `p ⊂ R` a prime
ideal such that the localization `R_p` is a discrete valuation ring and `p` is
analytically unramified (`R^ / p R^` is reduced). Then for every associated prime
`q` of the `R^`-module `R^ / p R^`, the local ring `(R^)_q` is a discrete
valuation ring. -/
@[stacks 032Z]
theorem exists_isDiscreteValuationRing_atPrime_of_analyticallyUnramified {R : Type*} [CommRing R]
  [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] (p : Ideal R)
    [p.IsPrime]
    -- (1) `R_p` is a discrete valuation ring (hence a domain).
    [IsDomain (Localization.AtPrime p)] (hdvr : IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime p))
    -- (2) `p` is analytically unramified: `R^ / p R^` is reduced.
    (hunr : AnalyticallyUnramifiedPrime p)
    -- `q` is an associated prime of the `R^`-module `R^ / p R^`.
    (q : Ideal (mCompletion R)) (hq : IsAssociatedPrime q (mCompletion R ⧸ pCompletion p)) :
    -- Conclusion: `(R^)_q` is a discrete valuation ring (in particular a domain).
    ∃ (_ : q.IsPrime) (_ : IsDomain (Localization.AtPrime q)),
      IsDiscreteValuationRing (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
  -- `q` is prime: this is the first component of `IsAssociatedPrime`.
  have hqprime : q.IsPrime := hq.isPrime
  refine ⟨hqprime, ?_⟩
  -- Step 1: `q` is minimal over `pCompletion p` (reduced ⇒ assoc = minimal).
  have hmin : q ∈ (pCompletion p).minimalPrimes := l1_assoc_minimal p hunr q hq
  -- Step 2: the maximal ideal of `(R^)_q` is the extension of `pCompletion p`.
  have hmax :
    (pCompletion p).map (algebraMap (mCompletion R) (Localization.AtPrime q)) =
      IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) :=
    l2_maximalIdeal_eq p q hunr hmin
  -- Step 3: a uniformizer `x ∈ R` whose image `x̄` generates the maximal ideal
  -- of `(R^)_q` and is *not nilpotent*.
  obtain ⟨x, hxnn, hxgen⟩ := l3_uniformizer p hdvr q hmax
  -- The maximal ideal is nonzero: it is `span {x̄}` with `x̄ ≠ 0` (n = 1 of
  -- non-nilpotency).
  have hne : IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal (Localization.AtPrime q) ≠ ⊥ := by
    rw [← hxgen]
    intro h
    have hx0 : algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q) x = 0 := by
      simpa using (Ideal.span_singleton_eq_bot).mp h
    exact hxnn 1 (by simpa using hx0)
  -- `(R^)_q` is Noetherian: `R^` is Noetherian (completion of a Noetherian local
  -- ring) and a localization of a Noetherian ring is Noetherian
  -- (`IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing`).
  have hNoeth : IsNoetherianRing (Localization.AtPrime q) := by
    -- `R^` is Noetherian (completion of a Noetherian local ring, Tag 0316), and a
    -- localization of a Noetherian ring is Noetherian.
    have : IsNoetherianRing (mCompletion R) := mCompletion_isNoetherianRing
    exact IsLocalization.isNoetherianRing q.primeCompl (Localization.AtPrime q) inferInstance
  -- Step 4: the image of `x` is a nonzerodivisor in `(R^)_q`, via the
  -- Krull-intersection regularity lemma (principal nonzero max ideal generated by
  -- a non-nilpotent element ⇒ that element is regular).
  have hxreg :
    algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q) x ∈ nonZeroDivisors (Localization.AtPrime q) :=
    regular_of_principal_maximalIdeal_of_not_nilpotent _ hxgen hxnn
  -- Step 5: assemble — `(R^)_q` is a DVR (and a domain).
  exact
    l5_assemble (Localization.AtPrime q) (algebraMap R (Localization.AtPrime q) x) hxreg hxgen hne
